@meta
id: 27-06
title: Drill — stop the comment spreading
chapter: 27
type: drill
skills: set-option
par: 44
minutes: 4
reps: 8
vscode: nothing — VS Code does this to you too, with no switch to find
open: order.service.ts

@brief
Eight times: take the `o` flag out of `formatoptions`, then open three
lines under the comment with `3o` and type the retry call once. Save, quit,
go again.

Leave the option alone and vim helpfully makes all three new lines
comments, because `formatoptions` contains `o`: "when `o` or `O` opens a
line below a comment, keep the comment going". Useful in prose. Infuriating
in code.

@keys
| `:setlocal formatoptions-=o` | drop one flag from the list |
| `:setlocal fo-=o` | the short name, for live use |
| `:set fo?` | read the flags back |

@hints
`formatoptions` is a list, so take the one flag out rather than assigning
a new value. The flag is the letter `o`.
--
`:setlocal fo-=o` then Enter, then `3oretry(payment);` and `Esc`.

@solution
    :setlocal fo-=o<Enter>  3oretry(payment);<Esc>  :wq<Enter>

Thirty-eight keystrokes.

`formatoptions` is the strangest of the list options: its items are single
letters with no commas between them, and there are about twenty of them.
Four are worth recognising on sight:

    r   Enter inside a comment keeps the comment going
    o   o and O below a comment keep the comment going
    t   wrap text at textwidth as you type
    c   wrap comments at textwidth as you type

`-=` works on it letter by letter, which is why `fo-=o` is safe and
`fo=tcq` would trample whatever the filetype plugin had decided.

Note the `setlocal`. `formatoptions` is set per buffer by whichever
filetype plugin loaded, so a global `:set fo-=o` gets overwritten the next
time you open a file of that type. The next few lessons are about exactly
that distinction.

@start order.service.ts
// eslint-disable-next-line @typescript-eslint/no-explicit-any
const handler = createHandler();

@expected order.service.ts
// eslint-disable-next-line @typescript-eslint/no-explicit-any
retry(payment);
retry(payment);
retry(payment);
const handler = createHandler();
